## 4. Selection and sizing

- Whether the project requires a partial discharge test at commissioning, which sets the workmanship standard.
- Pollution level for outdoor terminations at 35 kV, where shed profile has more influence than at 20 kV.
- Screen cut-back length and insulation diameter as measured on the actual cable.
- Wind or solar collection system layout, which often dictates a joint in a field rather than in a bay.
- Lead time against the project programme, since this class is usually specified on a critical path.

## 5. Standards commonly specified

- IEC 61442, test methods for power cable accessories above 3.6 kV up to 36 kV.
- IEC 60840, the cable standard for extruded insulation cables above 30 kV, relevant at the top of this class.
- IEEE Std 48, test procedures for AC cable terminations.
- IEC 60664-1, insulation coordination and creepage.

Standards are listed as those normally cited for this component class. They describe the requirement, not a claim of certification. Test evidence applicable to a specific order is confirmed per purchase order.

## 6. Handling and installation

- Work to a written procedure. At 35 kV the tolerance on screen cut-back and stress cone position is tighter than at 20 kV.
- Do not install in rain or in condensing humidity without a shelter over the joint bay.
- Verify the earthing of screen and armour before energisation and record the reading.
- Keep the recovered surface clean. At this stress level a surface contaminant can initiate tracking.

## 7. Failure modes and mitigation

| Failure mode | Likely cause | Mitigation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Partial discharge above the acceptance level | Installation tolerance in the stress control region | Follow the written procedure, work dry, and test at commissioning where specified. |
| Outdoor termination tracking | Pollution level higher than the shed profile was selected for | Select on the site pollution class and clean before energisation. |
| Sealing failure after field installation | Work carried out in wet or condensing conditions | Shelter the bay, dry the surfaces, and apply sealing parts to drawing. |
| Programme slippage | Accessory lead time not aligned with the cable delivery | Place the accessory order with the cable, not after it. |

## 8. Typical applications

- Wind farm and solar collection systems at 35 kV.
- Utility distribution and sub-transmission interfaces.
- MV cable manufacturers and renewable balance-of-system suppliers.
- Projects where a commissioning partial discharge test is part of the specification.

